# SRG-APP-000439-WSR-000188  -  CAT II
# The web server must remove all export ciphers to protect the
# confidentiality and integrity of transmitted information.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000439-WSR-000188
group:           V-206440
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-002418
control_rev5:    SC-8

contribution:    Splunk can replace the OpenSSL default cipher string with an explicit list
                 of approved AES with SHA-2 suites on every endpoint and can restrict
                 elliptic curve negotiation to the approved named curves, which removes
                 export and other weak ciphers from negotiation.

governs:         inputs.conf - Configures inputs, distributed inputs such as forwarders, and file system
                 monitoring.
governs:         outputs.conf - Where this instance forwards its data, and how that connection is
                 protected.
governs:         server.conf - Core server settings, including the certificates and protocols used to
                 protect management and replication traffic.
governs:         web.conf - Configures the Splunk Web interface.

check:           web.conf [settings] cipherSuite matches ^(TLS_AES_(128|256)_GCM_SHA(256|384)|((ECDHE|DHE)-(ECDSA|RSA)-)?AES(128|256)-(GCM-|CCM-)?SHA(256|384))(:(TLS_AES_(128|256)_GCM_SHA(256|384)|((ECDHE|DHE)-(ECDSA|RSA)-)?AES(128|256)-(GCM-|CCM-)?SHA(256|384)))*$
check:           server.conf [sslConfig] cipherSuite matches ^(TLS_AES_(128|256)_GCM_SHA(256|384)|((ECDHE|DHE)-(ECDSA|RSA)-)?AES(128|256)-(GCM-|CCM-)?SHA(256|384))(:(TLS_AES_(128|256)_GCM_SHA(256|384)|((ECDHE|DHE)-(ECDSA|RSA)-)?AES(128|256)-(GCM-|CCM-)?SHA(256|384)))*$
check:           inputs.conf [SSL] cipherSuite matches ^(TLS_AES_(128|256)_GCM_SHA(256|384)|((ECDHE|DHE)-(ECDSA|RSA)-)?AES(128|256)-(GCM-|CCM-)?SHA(256|384))(:(TLS_AES_(128|256)_GCM_SHA(256|384)|((ECDHE|DHE)-(ECDSA|RSA)-)?AES(128|256)-(GCM-|CCM-)?SHA(256|384)))*$
check:           outputs.conf [tcpout:<target_group>] cipherSuite not_matches (EXP-|RC4|RC2|DES-CBC|3DES|IDEA|SEED|CAMELLIA|PSK|-MD5|NULL|ADH-|AECDH-)|(^|:)(ALL|DEFAULT|COMPLEMENTOFALL|LOW|MEDIUM|HIGH)($|:)
check:           server.conf [sslConfig] ecdhCurves matches ^\s*prime256v1\s*,\s*secp384r1\s*,\s*secp521r1\s*$
