retired_check:   web.conf [settings] ecdhCurves matches ^\s*prime256v1\s*,\s*secp384r1\s*,\s*secp521r1\s*$
                 reason: 10.4.2 spec: "A list of ECDH curves to use for ECDH key
                         negotiation... The server supports only the curves specified in the
                         list. Splunk software only supports named curves that have been
                         specified by their SHORT names... Example setting: 'ecdhCurves =
                         prime256v1,secp384r1,secp521r1'. The default can vary." Vendor
                         page: the [sslConfig] setting "controls key exchange curves for TLS
                         1.2 connections", and for TLS 1.3 "the equivalent setting is
                         'groups' in the [tls1.3] stanza".
