external:        FIPS validated cryptographic module and OpenSSL build supplied by the host
                 operating system, which determines which of the listed suites are actually
                 available
external:        Client, peer and browser cipher preferences, which complete the
                 negotiation
external:        Any TLS terminating reverse proxy, whose own cipher list is outside the
                 application

citation:        SRG-APP-000439-WSR-000188 check text; SPLK-CL-000430 fix text;
                 web.conf.spec:255-296; server.conf.spec:940-970, 1036-1040;
                 inputs.conf.spec:1052-1060; outputs.conf.spec:664-669
finding:         A Splunk cipherSuite setting is absent or is an OpenSSL class string
                 rather than an explicit list of approved AES with SHA-2 suites, so export
                 and other weak ciphers remain available, or the ECDH curve list is not the
                 approved prime256v1, secp384r1, secp521r1 set.
